  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district, governmental funds only (no business-type funds). Receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (pp4-5); balance sheet from the net position section (p3). The statement's Total receipts 3,800,253 includes 90,000 Special Building loan proceeds (p15) that has no printed line on the statement (Special Building column lines sum to 137,803, printed 227,803); recorded as debt_proceeds and listed in reported_totals includes. Identity: 1,825,635 + 3,710,253 - 3,660,982 + 188,000 - 188,000 + 90,000 = 1,964,906. Transfers in (188,000) = Nutrition 93,000 + Activities 95,000, matching General Fund transfers out 188,000. A further 150,000 General Fund to Depreciation Fund transfer is inside the General Fund schedule's 2700 Pupil transportation line (229,786) and is reclassified on p9; both funds are General Fund components so it nets out of the statement; split out as other financing in detail (review). General Fund detail uses the budget and actual schedule (pp10-12, with budgets); the General Fund Components combining schedule (pp7-9) is the same data and is not recorded again. State programs 3,746 and federal programs 23,616 are reclassified into regular and special education instruction on the statement; all are category instruction. Postsecondary receipts, REAP, Community services budget-only lines have no actual and are skipped. Activities Fund prints one disbursement line (no per-account schedule). Read pages 1-16 of 16"
